{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"event driven agent pattern event driven agent pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md","fileName":"Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Event-Driven Agent Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"event driven agent pattern event driven agent pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md","fileName":"Event-Driven Agent Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Event-Driven Agent Pattern","heading":"Event-Driven Agent Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An event-driven agent is attached to a bounded platform event such as a pull-request opening, workflow failure, monitoring alert, or manual dispatch. The event determines what context may be retrieved; the agent reasons over that context; structured output is returned; and a deterministic policy gate selects the allowed response.\n\nThis pattern keeps agent activity attributable to a trigger and separates interpretation from action. Failure triage, pull-request review, verification loops, and alert investigations differ in context and permitted side effects, but each follows the same event, retrieval, reasoning, validation, and policy sequence.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsen